Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:59:01 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] test(coarse_laws): expect the STEP facet budget refusal
 wording (#1074)

coarse_laws.rs still built the refusal as "re-import with a larger budget";
since #1074 model_fidelity::TOO_COARSE says "a larger STEP facet budget".
Test-only; the refusal is unchanged. coarse_laws 6/6.

Fixes #1175

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL
---
 crates/app/tests/coarse_laws.rs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/crates/app/tests/coarse_laws.rs b/crates/app/tests/coarse_laws.rs
index ad325a1a0..ea0f10993 100644
--- a/crates/app/tests/coarse_laws.rs
+++ b/crates/app/tests/coarse_laws.rs
@@ -121,7 +121,7 @@ fn fidelity_lines(world: &World) -> Vec<String> {
 }
 
 fn refusal(op: &str, mm: &str) -> String {
-    format!("{op}: model 'bar' was imported too coarsely to verify; re-import with a larger budget (surfaces are approximated to within {mm} mm)")
+    format!("{op}: model 'bar' was imported too coarsely to verify; re-import with a larger STEP facet budget (surfaces are approximated to within {mm} mm)")
 }
 
 fn groove_finish(tolerance: f64) -> OpParams {
